<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 120,555 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 120,555 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 120,555 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 53,429 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			14,471	   11,359</p>
<p>    Import cargo		     106,084	   41,870</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, 10 ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Chemicals		 2,293	 NCC Jouf	     22/2</p>
<p>Crude oil		71,000	 Stavros-1	    22/2</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Warbah		 21/2</p>
<p>Feul oil		 60,000	 Al-Safa		24/2</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa	     24/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,500	 Bunga Cenderewasih 28/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
